      "size_x": 24,
      "size_y": 30,
      "visualization_settings": {
        "text": "# Glossary\nWhat every metric on this dashboard actually means.\n\n## Content Pipeline\n- **Total Unwatched Candidates**: movies and TV shows in the catalog that are not in your watch history yet. Books are counted separately under Unread Books.\n- **Unwatched Movies / Unwatched TV Shows**: same, split by type.\n- **Total Catalog Size**: distinct movies and TV shows ingested, watched or not.\n- **Last Pipeline Run**: timestamp of the most recent taste profile or recommendation refresh.\n- **Raw Rows Ingested**: total rows currently stored across all 7 raw tables (TMDB discovery and details, Simkl ratings, Hardcover ratings, and Open Library books).\n\n## Watch & Ratings\n- **Titles Rated**: movies/TV titles with a personal rating on record, all-time.\n- **Avg Rating**: average personal rating across all rated movies/TV titles, all-time.\n- **Rated This Month**: same, scoped to the current month.\n- **Most Watched Genre**: the genre with the most titles in your watch history, by count, not by average rating.\n- **Your Average Rating by Genre**: average rating per genre. A genre needs at least 2 ratings to appear, so one score cannot make or break a category.\n- **Top Platforms You Watch On**: platforms ranked by how many of your watched titles are streaming there in your region. Simkl doesn't record where you watched, so this is availability, not viewing.\n- **Content Consumed Per Month**: count of titles marked consumed, by the month watched.\n\n## Books\n- **Books Rated / Avg Book Rating / Books Rated This Month**: same pattern as Watch & Ratings, scoped to books.\n- **Unread Books**: books that can still be recommended (not read, not dismissed, and not another edition of a book already read).\n- **Your Average Rating by Book Subject**: average rating per subject tag. A subject needs at least 2 ratings to appear. Generic tags such as Fiction or New York Times bestseller are left out because most books carry them.\n\n## A note on freshness\nSimkl and Hardcover ingestion run on every pipeline run, but only register a change when the underlying rating data is actually different from what is already stored. A source with no recent activity reflects no new ratings upstream, not a broken pipeline.",
